                    <msContents>
                        <summary><p>Ricettario: in Italian and Latin.</p></summary>
                        <textLang mainLang="it" source="IANA">Italian</textLang>
                        <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_44_1">
                            <author>Ambrosius de Vigliano</author>
                            <title type="original">Ricettario</title>
                            <textLang mainLang="it" source="IANA">Italian</textLang>
                            <textLang mainLang="la" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
                            <filiation>The MS may have been written in a monastic house at Padua, as on fol. 123v, in the course of an entry concerning a 'Mirabile oleum Balsamicum', the writer states: 'Et vidi alium monachum nostrum qui defferendo magnam trabem cum aliis monachis in sancta Justina Paduae manum strinxit inter collonnas et trabem...'.</filiation>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc form="codex">
                            <supportDesc material="paper">
                                <extent>10[12] ll. + 131[132] ff. 4to.
                                    <dimensions type="leaf" unit="cm">
                                        <dim type="width">13 cm</dim>
                                        <dim type="length">18 cm</dim>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </extent>
                                <foliation>This manuscript contains early pagination for the main text and a later foliation for the whole manuscript.</foliation>
                                <collation>
                                    <p>First and last leaves of the first section, fol. 125, and last leaf missing.</p>
                                    <p>The first section (10 ll.) and ff. 109-end are on paper.</p>
                                </collation>            
                                <condition>Lower margin of fol. 111 torn away.</condition>
                            </supportDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote script="humanist">Written by several hands.</handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                        <decoDesc>
                            <decoNote type="rubrication">A few headings and paragraph marks in red.</decoNote>
                        </decoDesc>
                        <additions>In the upper margin of fol. 41 'Fra[ter] Ambrosius. or[dinis]. mi[norum]. Vigl[ia]nne[nsis]'. In the lower margin of the penultimate leaf of the first section is the name of 'Fratris Bernardini de Varallo ordinis minorum' in an early 16th cent. hand.</additions>
                        <bindingDesc>
                            <binding>
                                <p>On vellum and paper. Original stamped leather binding worn; both ties wanting.</p>
                            </binding>
                        </bindingDesc>
